{
  "_comment": [
    "The whole clip library for Adamant, authored as data (docs/skeleton.md conventions).",
    "",
    "Poses are joint -> {x,y,z} rotation OFFSETS FROM THE T-POSE REST, in degrees, exactly as",
    "docs/skeleton.md defines them. 'stance' is the named STANCE pose: the visual origin.",
    "",
    "Every clip key's 'pose' is a PARTIAL OVERRIDE ON TOP OF stance: a joint that is not",
    "mentioned holds its stance value. An empty pose {} therefore IS stance, which is how the",
    "'every clip starts and ends at STANCE' rule is enforced structurally rather than by hand",
    "(see tools/pose_check.py, which fails the build data if a non-terminal clip breaks it).",
    "",
    "'_root' is root motion: a translation offset of the Hips node in rig units (cm), in the",
    "fighter's own frame (+x = the fighter's left, +y = up, +z = toward the opponent).",
    "'_rootRot' is whole-body rotation in degrees, pre-multiplied onto the Hips rotation; it is",
    "root motion, not a pelvis bend, so it is not bound by the Hips range in the skeleton map.",
    "Neither has an entry in docs/skeleton.md's SKELETON_MAP — see SPEC_NOTES.md #2.",
    "",
    "'_fist' is how closed the hands are: 1 = the fist authored in skeleton-map.json's 'hand'",
    "section, 0 = the rig's own flat open rest hand, and {\"left\": n, \"right\": n} to drive one",
    "hand alone. Fifteen finger bones per hand are generated from it at load time, so a punch",
    "can clench on the way out without burying the pose that matters under finger rotations.",
    "",
    "'_root.y' is normally computed, not authored: clips with \"ground\": true (the default) get",
    "their hips height solved per keyframe at load time so the lowest toe stays on the canvas",
    "floor while the knees bend. 'ko' opts out and authors its own fall.",
    "",
    "'f' is a frame index at 30 fps; 'frames' is the clip length in frames.",
    "Clip name IS the action name from adamant_spec.md 2 — no mapping table anywhere."
  ],
