    "ko": {
      "_note": "Terminal — the only clip exempt from returning to STANCE. It is also the only clip that has to obey gravity, and the two failures it can have are opposites: a body that ploughs through the deck, and a body that descends at a constant rate and stops in the air. The second one is what a rigid backward tip about planted feet looks like, and it reads as sinking rather than falling. So: the legs buckle first and the fighter loses its height standing up, the hips then accelerate — 0.9 cm per frame, then 2.4, then 4.7 — while the fold in the knees swings the feet clear of the arc, the back lands at f26 and stops the fall dead, and the last third is dead weight settling: head rolling back onto the deck, arms and legs going slack. Run tools/pose_render.py ko --trace to see that column; a constant rate there is an elevator, not a fall. Root motion is hand-authored (grounding off), which makes the leg fold load-bearing: the hips rotate ~90 degrees about a point the legs have to swing clear of. Verified on the skinned mesh, not the toe joints — tools/pose_check.py check 7, which also asserts that the settled body is ON the deck.",
